  "Question": "Which of these five numbers is the largest?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(13579 + \\dfrac{1}{2468} \\)",
    "B": "\\(13579 - \\dfrac{1}{2468} \\)",
    "C": "\\(13579 \\times \\dfrac{1}{2468} \\)",
    "D": "\\(13579 \\div \\dfrac{1}{2468} \\)",
    "E": "\\(13579.2468 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Since \\(0<\\frac1{2468}<1\\), subtracting this fraction from \\(13579\\) or multiplying \\(13579\\) by it gives a number below \\(13579\\). Adding it gives a number below \\(13580\\), and \\(13579.2468\\) is also below \\(13580\\).\n\nDividing by a nonzero fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal. Therefore choice D is\n\\[\n13579\\div\\frac1{2468}=13579\\times2468\n>13579\\times2=27158.\n\\]\nThis exceeds every other choice, so the largest number is \\(\\boxed{13579\\div\\frac1{2468}}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
